# Code Simplification — {{project_name}}

<!-- GEN: Why: the agent must see when to run, the loop and the hard limits at once, because a simplification done at the wrong time or too far is a bug. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->
<!-- GEN: Description: follow ~/.claude/skill-factory/core/authoring-guide.md "Description" — workspace name, concrete situations, the team's own trigger words (their language allowed), an "even if" clause; check it against the trial prompts (Step 8). -->

Goal: code a newcomer understands on first read — not the fewest lines. A change is a simplification only when a reader holds **fewer concepts** afterwards.

## 1. The loop

1. Checks are green; take only the phase's diff ([01]({{ref_01}})).
2. Understand callers, side effects, error paths and tests ([01]({{ref_01}})).
3. Pass the diff through the four lenses — **Reuse, Simplification, Efficiency, Altitude** — and name each smell from the catalog; skip code that is already clear ([02]({{ref_02}})).
4. One small simplification → rerun `{{check_commands}}` (`PASS` / `FAIL`).
5. Stop at the stop criteria; findings that would change behavior or reach outside the diff go to Concerns ([01]({{ref_01}})).
6. Report one `simplify:` line ([03]({{ref_03}})).

